[[File:Demonic Pacts - Overview (1).png|thumb|600px|center|If you can't see the asset above, [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-08/DP-Tree.png click here].]]
We're here to give you all you need to know about this new take on combat for Leagues VI. While Yama has given you plenty of generous options for power this time around, your soul will belong to him by the end of this league.

Before we dive in, we want to make it '''clear''' that this system is being tested right up until launch, so there may be some instances where we slightly tweak numbers or descriptions. In that case we will let you know and update the [https://tools.runescape.wiki/demonic-pacts OSRS Wiki Calculator], which will be the source of truth.

==Overview==
For those of you who either haven't played a league before, missed Leagues V: Raging Echoes or forgot what Combat Masteries were, they essentially gave you a variety of specific combat buffs over the three main styles of Magic, Melee and Ranged.

While the previous league gave you a total of 18 choices over three different paths, this time around you've got '''over 130''' to choose from. These do stick to the same three styles but we've also sprinkled in some neutral nodes which don't give any specific style a buff but are there to enhance your builds in different ways.

[[File:Demonic Pacts - Overview (2).png|thumb|600px|center|If you can't see the asset above, [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-08/DP-Tooltip.png click here].]]
You can access the Demonic Pacts in the Leagues Menu through the 'Demonic Pacts' button and explore the tree at your own leisure. You'll also have a small tutorial at the end that will give you an overview of the system.

[[File:Demonic Pacts - Overview (3).png|thumb|201px|center|If you can't see the asset above, [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-08/Leagues-Panel-1.png click here].]]
You'll also have a handy summary of everything you've unlocked on the right-hand side!

[[File:Demonic Pacts - Overview (4).png|thumb|600px|center|If you can't see the asset above, [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-08/DP-Summary.png click here].]]

===Pact Points===
Unlocking pacts are done with Pact Points, with nodes only being available to unlock if an adjacent node has already been unlocked.

[[File:Demonic Pacts - Overview (5).png|thumb|600px|center|If you can't see the asset above, [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-08/DP-Points.png click here].]]

These points will be your currency to unlock your Demonic Pacts. Each pact will cost 1 point and if you gain all of them, you'll have a total of '''40 Pact Points!'''

We've split them out across the different areas which means you'll get:

* 9 from global tasks (with 2 given during the tutorial)
* 4 from Varlamore
* 6 from Karamja
* 7 for each additional area unlocked

You'll always begin at the centre of the tree and spend your first point on that pact, but after this and as long as you have at least one connected pact unlocked, you can go wherever you like on the 'tree'!

Much like last year's Masteries, these can be achieved through specific tasks related to combat. We've even included a handy little filter in the task interface to show you the specific tasks you need to complete for points.

[[File:Demonic Pacts - Overview (6).png|thumb|600px|center|If you can't see the asset above, [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-04-08/DP-Tasks.png click here].]]

